          beforeLabel: "Typical responsibilities:",
          after: null,
          afterLabel: null,
          extraCode: "Amazon EC2\nMicrosoft Azure Virtual Machines\nGoogle Compute Engine\nDigitalOcean Droplets",
          extraLabel: "Common providers:",
          note: "IaaS offers maximum flexibility... but also maximum responsibility."
        },
        {
          title: "2. PaaS — Platform as a Service",
          before: "Push code\n↓\nPlatform builds application\n↓\nDeploy\n↓\nApplication is online",
          beforeLabel: "Typical workflow:",
          after: "Vercel\nRender\nRailway\nHeroku",
          afterLabel: "Examples:",
          extraCode: null,
          extraLabel: null,
          note: "This is exactly why I enjoy deploying my portfolio on Vercel. I don't need to configure Linux. I don't need to install Node. I don't need to worry about web servers. I simply focus on building the application."
        },
        {
          title: "3. SaaS — Software as a Service",
          before: null,
          beforeLabel: null,
          after: "GitHub\nNotion\nFigma\nSlack\nGoogle Docs\nCanva",
          afterLabel: "Examples:",
          extraCode: null,
          extraLabel: null,
          note: "This one is actually the easiest. You don't build the software. You simply use it. The provider manages everything. You only need an account."
        },
        {
          title: "4. Real examples from my own projects",
          before: "Vue\n↓\nVercel (PaaS)\n↓\nCustom Domain",
          beforeLabel: "While building my portfolio, my stack looked something like this:",
